{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit makes it easy to sync data between the main app and its keyboard extension, by setting up an App Group and adding that information to your "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 1. Create an App Group","anchor":"Step-1-Create-an-App-Group","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You must first create an App Group in the Apple Developer Portal, under Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles. Select “Identifiers” and tap the plus button to add a new App Group with the name “group.<your-apps-bundle-id>”."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"developer-data-sync-developer-portal"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"macOS App Groups must start with Team ID instead of “group.”. This means that you must use different groups on iOS and macOS.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"important","type":"aside"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 2. Add the App Group to all targets","anchor":"Step-2-Add-the-App-Group-to-all-targets","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After creating your new App Group, you must enable it for both your app and its keyboard extension, under “Signing & Capabilites”."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"developer-data-sync-xcode-app"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It’s important to enable the App Group for all targets that will share data, otherwise the data will not be synced across all targets.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"important","type":"aside"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 3. Set up KeyboardKit to use the App Group","anchor":"Step-3-Set-up-KeyboardKit-to-use-the-App-Group","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To use the App Group with KeyboardKit, just add it to the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp\/appGroupId","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" in the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" you use to set up KeyboardKit. This will replace the main setting "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardSettings\/store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with a store that syncs changes between the main app and its keyboard."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"developer-data-sync-keyboard-app"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Getting-Started-Article","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" guide shows you how to create an app-specific "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value and use it to set up your app and keyboard."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Manual Setup (Optional)","anchor":"Manual-Setup-Optional","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you don’t want to use a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to set up data sync, you can set up the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardSettings","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" settings "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardSettings\/store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" manually as well. Just set the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardSettings\/store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to a custom "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Foundation\/UserDefaults","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that is configured to sync data in a way that fits your needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you set up data sync manually, you have to make sure that the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardSettings\/store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is properly configured in both the app and the keyboard."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-data-syncing"]},{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-data-syncing"]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Articles"],["doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles","doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Settings-Article"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"This developer guide describes how to sync data between the main app and its keyboard.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"images":[{"type":"card","identifier":"Dev